rs a mile of beach for swimming, surf fishing, tidepool exploring and camping. The Spanish named the area Carpinteria because the Chumash tribe, which lived in the area, had a large seagoing canoe-building enterprise, or &quot;carpentry shop&quot; there. The tribe had chosen the location because of naturally-occurring surface tar which was used to seal the boats.  Seals and sea lions can be seen in the area December through May, as well as an occasional gray whale.  Tidepools contain starfish, sea anemones, crabs, snails, octopi and sea urchin.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Body surfing<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Group Camping<br>Hiking<br>Picnic area<br>Playground<br>Scuba diving<br>Surfing<br>Swimming<br>Visitor Center<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=599", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/6.jpg", "BannerUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/banner6.jpg", "ParkSize": "Small", "Latitude": 34.39246482, "Longitude": -119.5210224, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:54", "MilesFromSelected": 0, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": false, "ParkCategoryId": 2, "ParkActivity": 1, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-22T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {"357": {"FacilityId": 357, "Name": "Anacapa (sites 101-127 & group sites)", "Description": "Anacapa (sites 101-127 & group sites)", "RateMessage": "Starting at $10.00", "FacilityType": 2, "FacilityTypeNew": 1, "InSeason": true, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 30, "IsRestricti