f the coast was first called gaviota (seagull) by soldiers of the Portola Expedition in 1769. A pier on the west end of the beach is used by divers and surfers. A Southern Pacific railroad trestle crosses the creek above the day-use parking lot. Visitors can explore the upland portions of the park from a trailhead in the parking area. Gaviota Peak offers a view of the coast and the Channel Islands.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Boating<br>Body surfing<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Hiking<br>Horseback riding<br>Picnic area<br>Rinse Showers<br>Scuba diving<br>Store-convenience<br>Surfing<br>Swimming<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=606", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/646.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 34.47315079, "Longitude": -120.2294715, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:54", "MilesFromSelected": 41, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": false, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-22T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 665, "Name": "Leo Carrillo SP", "Description": "The Park has 1.5 miles of beach to explore reefs, tidepools, coastal caves, fish, and surf. Giant sycamores shade the main campgrounds. The park offers hiking, a visitor center, camp store, and welcomes dogs on a leash in specified areas. Junior Ranger & campfire programs are offered in the summer.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=616", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/665.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Small", "Latitude": 34.04416667, "Longitude": -118.9383333, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:54", "MilesFromSelected": 42, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": false, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 1, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-22T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 1138, "Name": "Hungry Valley SVRA", "Description": "Hungry Valley SVRA", "HasAlerts": false, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Birdwatching<br>Camping<br>Group Camping<br>Hiking<br>Horseback riding<br>Off Road Vehicles<br>Visitor Center<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=1192", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/1138.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Small", "Latitude": 34.7920049, "Longitude": -118.8710124, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:54", "MilesFromSelected": 47, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 4, "ParkActivity": 2, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 30, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 644, "Name": "Fort Tejon SHP", "Description": "Fort Tejon State Historic Park is the site of a fort established by the U.S. Army in 1854. The post is one of the significant remaining links to the early American occupation period of California. The fort was designed to protect Native Americans living on the Sebastian Indian Reservation.  There a restored adobes from the original fort and the park's museum features exhibon army life and local history. The park also has a number of beautiful 400 year-old valley oak trees. The site also has living history events held by volunteers in costume.", "HasAlerts": false, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Birdwatching<br>Camping<br>Group Camping<br>Hiking<br>Horseback riding<br>Picnic area<br>Visitor Center<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=585", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/644.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 34.87480491, "Longitude": -118.8930124, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:54", "MilesFromSelected": 49, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 3, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 30, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 670, "Name": "Malibu Creek SP", "Description": "The park has over 4,000 acres and 15 miles of trails with a creek, rock pool, lake, chaparrals and many trees. Visitors can enjoy hiking, biking, swimming, and fishing. The park was home to Native American’s for centuries and used for filming hits such as Planet of the Apes and M*A*S*H.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Birdwatching<br>Boating<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Group Camping<br>Hiking<br>Horseback riding<br>Picnic area<br>Swimming<br>Visitor Center<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=614", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/670.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 34.10077346, "Longitude": -118.7113421, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:54", "MilesFromSelected": 51, "Available": true, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 1, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-22T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": true, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": true}, {"PlaceId": 686, "Name": "Oceano Dunes SVRA", "Description": "Oceano Dunes State Vehicular Recreation Area has 1,500 acres, featuring beach and sand dune riding.  Thousands of off-highway vehicle enthusiasts enjoy the beach dunes of this SVRA most weekends during the summer. It is a motorcycle, four-wheel drive, all-terrain vehicle, and dune buggy use area. Camping is allowed on the beach.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Birdwatching<br>Boating<br>Body surfing<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Group Camping<br>Hiking<br>Horseback riding<br>Off Road Vehicles<br>Rinse Showers<br>Scuba diving<br>Store-convenience<br>Surfing<br>Swimming<br>", "Url": "http://www.ohv.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=1207", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/686.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 35.09321039, "Longitude": -120.6178957, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:54", "MilesFromSelected": 79, "Available": true, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 4, "ParkActivity": 1, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 241, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-22T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 30, "IsRestrictionValid": true, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 691, "Name": "Pismo SB", "Description": "Pismo State Beach offers all kinds of attractions: hiking, swimming and surf fishing; the annual winter migration of millions of monarch butterflies (the park has the largest over-wintering colony of monarch butterflies in the U.S.); and tree-lined beach is also popular with bird watchers. Ocean Lagoon has a wheelchair-accessible fishing overhang.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Birdwatching<br>Boating<br>Body surfing<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Golf course<br>Hiking<br>Horseback riding<br>Scuba diving<br>Surfing<br>Swimming<br>Visitor Center<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=595", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/691.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 35.10640682, "Longitude": -120.6270577, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:54", "MilesFromSelected": 80, "Available": true, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 2, "ParkActivity": 1, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 1, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-22T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 15, "IsRestrictionValid": true, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 619, "Name": "Bolsa Chica SB", "Description": "Bolsa Chica State Beach is a popular place for surf fishing for perch, corbina, croaker, cabezon and sand shark.  Also popular in the summer is bare-handed fishing for California grunion, a species that only spawns on southern California beaches.  The beach extends three miles from Seal Beach to Huntington Beach City Pier.  A bikeway connects it with Huntington State Beach, seven miles south.  Wildlife and bird watching are popular.  Across the road from the beach is the 1,000-acre Bolsa Chica Ecological Reserve, operated by the California Dept. of Fish and Game.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Body surfing<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Hiking<br>Picnic area<br>Rinse Showers<br>Surfing<br>Swimming<br>Visitor Center<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=642", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/619.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Small", "Latitude": 33.69499752, "Longitude": -118.0468583, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:54", "MilesFromSelected": 98, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": false, "ParkCategoryId": 2, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-22T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 679, "Name": "Montana De Oro SP", "Description": "Montana de Oro State Park features over 8,000 acres of rugged cliffs, secluded sandy beaches,\r\n coastal plains, streams, canyons, and hills - with 1,347-foot Valencia Peak. Naturalists and backpackers enjoy the solitude and \r\n freedom found along the park trails. There are also mountain biking and equestrian trails. The best-known beach is Spooner's Cove,\r\n across from the campground. The park's name (Mountain of Gold) comes from the golden wildflowers that bloom in spring.\r\n  Wildlife in the park includes black tailed deer and the black oystercatcher. The park includes primitive and equestrian campsites.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Boating<br>Body surfing<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Hiking<br>Horseback riding<br>Picnic area<br>Scuba diving<br>Surfing<br>Visitor Center<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=592", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/679.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 35.26388889, "Longitude": -120.8622222, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:54", "MilesFromSelected": 98, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 1, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 680, "Name": "Morro Bay SP", "Description": "Morro Bay State Park features lagoon and natural bay habitat. The bay's most prominent landmark is Morro Rock. The park has opportunities for sailing fishing, hiking, and bird watching. The park museum has exhibits that cover natural features and cultural history, Native American life, geology, and oceanography. The park also has a colorful marina and an 18-hole public golf course. On the bay's northeast edge is a pristine saltwater marsh that supports a thriving bird population.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Birdwatching<br>Boating<br>Boat launch<br>Body surfing<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Golf course<br>Group Camping<br>Hiking<br>Museum<br>Picnic area<br>Rinse Showers<br>Surfing<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=594", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/680.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Small", "Latitude": 35.34653383, "Longitude": -120.8419937, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:54", "MilesFromSelected": 100, "Available": true, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 1, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-22T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 10, "IsRestrictionValid": true, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": true}, {"PlaceId": 702, "Name": "Saddleback Butte SP", "Description": "Saddleback Butte State Park was established in 1960 to preserve its high-desert Joshua tree woodland. To the east of the campground and picnic area rises 3,651-foot Saddleback Butte. Key park attractions are the short self-guided Dic Dowen Nature Trail, the Peak Trail climbing 1,000 feet to a dramatic view across the Western Mojave Desert, a Visitor Center featuring natural and cultural history displays, and the unique Joshua Tree/Creosote habitat found only in the Mojave Desert. Springtime brings a show of wildflowers that varies yearly, and fall has clear skies and pleasant temperatures. Summer days are hot but nights are warm with excellent stargazing. Wildlife includes Mountain Bluebirds, Kit Foxes, and the federally-threatened Desert Tortoise.", "HasAlerts": false, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Birdwatching<br>Camping<br>Group Camping<br>Hiking<br>Horseback riding<br>Picnic area<br>Visitor Center<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=618", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/702.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 34.67777778, "Longitude": -117.8041667, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:14:54", "MilesFromSelected": 100, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 30, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}]}, "part": "place-6"}